Subject: [PATCH 1/3] util/amdfwtool: Add UMC firmware type and a CyanSkillfish
 platform

The ASRock BC-250's stock BIOS (AMD Cyan Skillfish, family 17h model
47h) carries a PSP directory entry of type 0x4F holding the UMC
(memory controller) firmware, which amdfwtool did not know. Add it as
AMD_FW_PSP_UMC_FW / PSP_UMC_FW_FILE.

Also add a CyanSkillfish platform. Its stock layout is Picasso's
(single-level directories, pre-second-gen EFS) except that it has no
soft fuse chain entry and no PSB signature slot, and it ships the
secure debug key and debug unlock entries without a debug unlock.
Allow a platform to opt out of the soft fuse chain, and skip the
BIOS signature entry when the platform reserves no space for it.

